# Model routing policy (Kimi-first)

You are a coding agent working in this repository.

## Primary model strategy
- IF task risk is low/medium and scope is local, THEN use Kimi K2.6.
- IF Kimi iteration count >= 2 and errors are not decreasing, THEN switch to Sonnet 4.6.
- IF task touches >= 5 core files, or requires architectural refactor, THEN switch to Sonnet 4.6.
- IF change is high-risk (critical paths, fragile legacy behavior, unclear root cause after Sonnet), THEN switch to Opus 4.6.

## Handoff on model switch
When switching models, include:
- Goal and acceptance criteria.
- Summary of attempts and why they failed.
- Exact errors/logs observed.
- Files changed and pending files.
- Non-negotiable constraints (APIs, behavior, performance).

## Execution quality gate
- Never mark as complete without verification (tests/lint/run relevant to the change).
- If verification cannot run, explicitly state what is unverified and the exact command to validate.
- Prefer minimal diffs and avoid unrelated refactors.
- Preserve public APIs unless explicitly requested.

## Convergence policy
- Each iteration must reduce real failures, not just rewrite code.
- Stop broad rewrites if failing; isolate root cause and patch the smallest viable surface.
